.TH AD_SNAPSHOT 1 "2026-08-21" "ad 2.0" "ad scripts"
.SH NAME
ad_snapshot \- per-op HTML snapshots for documentation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_snapshot
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NAME\fR
    snapshot_per_op.sh — Per-op HTML snapshot visualizer for diffvim\fR
\fR
SYNOPSIS\fR
    snapshot_per_op.sh [-h|--help]\fR
    snapshot_per_op.sh [options] <oldfile> <newfile>\fR
\fR
DESCRIPTION\fR
    Runs the ad_vim pipeline (compute → postprocess → pace) on an\fR
    old/new file pair, then takes a snapshot of the animator's buffer\fR
    after every keep / delete / insert op and renders all those\fR
    snapshots into a single browsable HTML page (one entry per op,\fR
    with the changed character highlighted).\fR
\fR
    The HTML page is written to /tmp/ad_snapshots/snapshots.html —\fR
    open it in a browser to step through the animation op-by-op.\fR
\fR
OPTIONS\fR
    -h, --help              Show this help message and exit 0.\fR
    --show-keep             Show keep ops (default: hidden). When\fR
                            hidden, each delete/insert entry still\fR
                            shows the buffer state (the result after\fR
                            the op was applied).\fR
    --show-pacing           Include delay ops in the output\fR
                            (default: excluded).\fR
    --context N             Show only N lines of context around the\fR
                            changed line (default: -1 = show whole\fR
                            buffer; 0 = show only the changed line).\fR
    --frame-op              Show a frame/border around each op entry\fR
                            (default: off).\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show detailed help and exit
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ad_vim (1)
